<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  macOS camera/microphone usage descriptions for the Tauri desktop app. Without these, macOS's
  TCC (Transparency, Consent, and Control) privacy system has no description to show the user and
  denies the request outright rather than prompting -- exactly the reported symptom: RealtimeKit's
  Core SDK failing with "[ERR0001]: Failed to initialize. device not supported" when starting a
  video call from the Tauri window, and no permission dialog ever appearing at all.

  Tauri looks for a file literally named Info.plist / Info.macos.plist in the same directory as
  tauri.conf.json (this one) and merges it into the app's own Info.plist. The equivalent
  ios/App/App/Info.plist entry (added during Phase C for QR scanning) is a COMPLETELY SEPARATE
  file for the Capacitor iOS build -- this app has TWO independent native shells (Tauri desktop,
  Capacitor mobile), each needing its own platform-specific permission declarations.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>NSCameraUsageDescription</key>
    <string>ClinüxFlow uses the camera for video consultations between care team members and for scanning session-transfer QR codes.</string>
    <key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
    <string>ClinüxFlow uses the microphone for video consultations between care team members.</string>
</dict>
</plist>
